#
# Counter-example for the reasoned-graph math: expression-identity gate
# (crates/logic/src/math_expression.rs, classify_structural_key_usage /
# check_malformed_structural_key): TWO well-formed math:NumberLiteral roots, each
# carrying a math:structuralKey usage that is NOT a well-formed singleton literal —
# ex:twoKeys asserts two literal values (a plural key: which one is "the" digest?),
# ex:nonLiteralKey asserts one value that is an IRI rather than a literal at all. Both
# lower cleanly (NumberLiteral needs only math:literalValue), so neither is a rejected
# expression, and neither carries a single clean literal a drift check could compare —
# both MUST raise ONLY math:MalformedStructuralKey (never math:StructuralKeyDrift or
# math:StructuralKeyOnRejectedExpression).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:twoKeys a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:literalValue 1 ;
    math:structuralKey "not-the-real-digest-1" , "not-the-real-digest-2" .

ex:nonLiteralKey a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:literalValue 2 ;
    math:structuralKey ex:notALiteral .

ex:notALiteral a ex:Placeholder .
